    description: "PR 5 (WI-podor) labels Swift scopes by their enclosing callable, so same-named locals in two inits, overloads, accessors or subscripts no longer tie. Two Swift forms still tie, each fixed so far only by the occurrence split:\n\n1. Locals of two unbound closures, e.g. `.run { func h() }` twice in one body, or of two plain blocks in one body. There is no name to label the scope with.\n2. Locals of `func f()` and `func f() async`. `async` (and `throws`?) are not in the scope label. Verified on a fixture, where both `T.h` are hgstableid16:0754e5404cf2466f; not counted on real repositories.\n\nFound by PR 5 agent 1. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/podor/RESULTS.md."  # 747b
